WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.897
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.375
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:15.425
Unit eight: Urban Challenges. In this unit, you will discuss city problems using formal reporting structures.

4
00:00:16.417 --> 00:00:17.534
urbanisation.

5
00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:22.114
urbanisation means the movement of people from the countryside to cities.

6
00:00:22.414 --> 00:00:25.099
Rapid urbanisation is changing Cambodia.

7
00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:27.894
Your turn. Say: urbanisation.

8
00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:31.885
urbanisation.

9
00:00:32.883 --> 00:00:34.070
infrastructure.

10
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:38.778
infrastructure means basic systems like roads, water and electricity.

11
00:00:39.078 --> 00:00:40.997
The city needs better infrastructure.

12
00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:44.442
Your turn. Say: infrastructure.

13
00:00:47.142 --> 00:00:48.514
infrastructure.

14
00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:50.750
gentrification.

15
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.899
gentrification means when richer people move into a poor area and prices rise.

16
00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:59.151
Gentrification has pushed many families out of the centre.

17
00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:02.283
Your turn. Say: gentrification.

18
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:06.297
gentrification.

19
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:08.586
traffic congestion.

20
00:01:09.286 --> 00:01:12.563
traffic congestion means too many vehicles on the roads.

21
00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:16.105
Traffic congestion costs the city millions of hours.

22
00:01:16.805 --> 00:01:19.422
Your turn. Say: traffic congestion.

23
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:23.646
traffic congestion.

24
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:25.883
urban sprawl.

25
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:30.266
urban sprawl means the uncontrolled spread of a city into the countryside.

26
00:01:30.566 --> 00:01:32.879
Urban sprawl is destroying farmland.

27
00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:36.626
Your turn. Say: urban sprawl.

28
00:01:39.326 --> 00:01:40.629
urban sprawl.

29
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:42.885
affordable housing.

30
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:47.581
affordable housing means homes that people on average incomes can pay for.

31
00:01:47.881 --> 00:01:49.800
There is a shortage of affordable housing.

32
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.163
Your turn. Say: affordable housing.

33
00:01:55.863 --> 00:01:57.329
affordable housing.

34
00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.016
slum.

35
00:01:59.716 --> 00:02:02.876
slum means a very poor and crowded area of a city.

36
00:02:03.176 --> 00:02:05.153
Many slums have no clean water.

37
00:02:05.853 --> 00:02:08.192
Your turn. Say: slum.

38
00:02:10.892 --> 00:02:11.777
slum.

39
00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:13.784
commuter belt.

40
00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:17.900
commuter belt means the area around a city where commuters live.

41
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.490
Prices are rising in the commuter belt too.

42
00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.692
Your turn. Say: commuter belt.

43
00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:27.509
commuter belt.

44
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:30.470
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.580
It is said that Phnom Penh's population will double by 2040.

46
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:38.861
That's huge! Is the infrastructure ready?

47
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.613
Not yet. Traffic congestion is thought to cost millions of dollars a year.

48
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:49.356
And affordable housing is said to be very difficult to find.

49
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:54.542
Gentrification is believed to be pushing families into the commuter belt.

50
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.302
So urban planning must improve quickly.

51
00:02:59.617 --> 00:03:02.638
Grammar focus: Passive reporting structures.

52
00:03:02.938 --> 00:03:06.273
Use passive reporting structures in formal writing and news.

53
00:03:06.573 --> 00:03:09.594
It is said that, or subject plus is said to plus verb.

54
00:03:09.894 --> 00:03:15.170
For example: It is said that the city is growing fast. The city is said to be growing fast.

55
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:20.059
These structures are common in news reports when the speaker is unknown or not important.

56
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:24.202
Now read and listen. Growing Cities, Growing Problems.

57
00:03:24.502 --> 00:03:27.662
Asia's cities are said to be the fastest-growing in the world.

58
00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:33.631
Urbanisation brings jobs and opportunities, but also serious challenges.

59
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:38.507
Traffic congestion and urban sprawl are believed to be getting worse.

60
00:03:39.817 --> 00:03:43.964
It is estimated that millions of people live in slums without proper infrastructure.

61
00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.956
Many experts think affordable housing is the key to fairer cities.

62
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.554
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:52.854 --> 00:03:55.666
Basic systems like roads and water are blank.

64
00:03:55.966 --> 00:04:00.281
A, infrastructure. B, urban sprawl. C, slums.

65
00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:06.608
The answer is A: infrastructure.

66
00:04:08.117 --> 00:04:10.372
It blank that the bridge will open next year.

67
00:04:10.672 --> 00:04:13.687
A, says. B, is said. C, said.

68
00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:19.288
The answer is B: is said.

69
00:04:20.783 --> 00:04:23.027
He is thought blank the richest man in town.

70
00:04:23.327 --> 00:04:26.040
A, to be. B, being. C, be.

71
00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.446
The answer is A: to be.

72
00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.006
When richer people move into a poor area, it is blank.

73
00:04:36.306 --> 00:04:40.586
A, gentrification. B, urbanisation. C, commuter belt.

74
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.629
The answer is A: gentrification.

75
00:04:48.117 --> 00:04:52.276
According to the text, which cities are said to be the fastest-growing?

76
00:04:52.576 --> 00:04:55.776
A, European. B, Asian. C, American.

77
00:04:59.783 --> 00:05:01.469
The answer is B: Asian.

78
00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:06.936
Now it's your turn to speak. What is the biggest challenge facing your city?

79
00:05:12.236 --> 00:05:18.752
It is often said that traffic congestion is our biggest problem, and I think affordable housing is a close second.

80
00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.633
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:25.730
Great work today! You learned eight new words and passive reporting structures.

82
00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:29.194
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

83
00:05:29.494 --> 00:05:31.670
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

84
00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.762
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

